// UNWRAP OF A POINTER IS READ TWO WAYS, BOTH KEPT: the alias pass walks a function as main does, an unwrap no step and the place under it its root
// whole, and when that walk met an unwrap of a pointer it walks the function again with every unwrap a step to its operand (the longer path, which
// re-roots through the pointer), one report per site; escape roots a view through a local's or a field's unwrap too, and an unwrap whose value is
// itself a wrapped pointer steps as well. THE PRICES AT PARITY (l.23411 item 5, l.23500 item 5, l.23643 ruled item 4, l.23798 item 4), each with a
// twin refused on main: `p3_z54o` (main's own `z54q_ok` case was here at row 10 and went back to
// tests/backend/programs/store_through_pointer_value_ok.npk at row 11, which accepts it again, l.23411 items 5 and 6); the self-pointing set's
// `ap3_rp_u`; interaction 1's four; this row's own `afa_q_hl_ok`; the computed pair under an unwrap. The cases from cells have each declared name
// suffixed by the cell's, in the form of main's prices files.
